  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard endings in every tense, no exceptions.",
    "Not reflexive: *bañar* means to bathe someone or something else (a baby, a dog). The reflexive form *bañarse* (\"to bathe oneself / take a bath\") is a separate verb file if needed.",
    "*Voy a bañar al perro esta tarde.* (\"I'm going to bathe the dog this afternoon.\")",
    "*Mi madre me bañaba cuando era pequeño.* (\"My mom used to bathe me when I was little.\")",
    "Related: *bañarse* (reflexive, \"to bathe oneself\"), *el baño* (bathroom / bath), *la bañera* (bathtub)."
  ],
